{"slug":"juiced-2","title":"Juiced 2","desc":"PC, THQ 2006 (Hot Import Nights)","notes":["Juiced 2: Hot Import Nights (PC, THQ 2006), read from cars/<car>.jfs (+ .jfshdr) with the Blender importer import_jfs.py (Ekey's JCED2.JFS.Tool formats). 93 cars; folder names are the archive names.  The stock car: body, glass, lights, interior, wheels with tyres, exhaust, mirrors (the game has no mesh LODs).","Paint: the game paints body and plastic parts with one colour at run time: here one red.","KITS: every aftermarket part of the shop (front / rear bumpers, side skirts, spoilers, bonnets, boot lids, roof parts, widebody shells and mirrors: <CAR>_<PART>_VS<n> / _WIDE<n>; the exhausts <CAR>_EXHAUST[_TWIN|_CENTRE]_<n>) is in the hidden 'Variants' folder of <car>.fbx (a subfolder per part, every part at its place on the car) and, to be seen, in <car>_kits.fbx: the stock car and one complete car per kit number (kit_vs<n> / kit_wide<n>: the parts of that number replace the stock ones; exhausts not used there), all VISIBLE, in rows of 6.","RIMS: _Rims holds the rims of the shop (shared.jfs: wheel_<brand>_<model>) and the stock rim of every car (stock_<car>: the rim named by the car's setup in scripts.jfs, FWHEELS = WHEEL_<CAR>), one per folder, at the game's common rim size (the game scales them per car), standing on the ground, outer face towards +X.  Rims only: the setups name a tyre profile, no tyre model was found in the archives.  Motion blur discs left out.","The wheels ON the cars are the car archives' own wheel models (WHEEL_FL ...: rim + tyre at the size of the car; the 350z's is another design than its stock rim).  tiburon and scion have no wheel models of their own (tiburon: 5 cm placeholder squares), so they stand without wheels.","Not included: the tuning-screen engine models, hidden damage and glow parts (all in the archives and available in the importer)."],"tags":["juiced-2"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["200sx","",14008455,"juiced-2","car-2